{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-318660" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Suppose we would like to find an integrating factor to convert the differential equation\n\n$$\n{y}^{3}\\,\\text{d}x+xy\\,\\text{d}y=0,\\,y>0\n$$\n\ninto an exact equation using an integrating factor. Select the correct options in the reasoning below. For a differential equation of the form\n\n$$\nP(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x+Q(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y=0,\n$$\n\nwe have that if\n\n$$\n{{field-1}}=h(y)\n$$\n\nwhere $h(y)$ is independent of $x,$ then an integrating factor for the equation is\n\n$$\nI(y)={{field-2}}\n$$\n\nwhere $\\operatorname{exp}⁡(y)$ denotes the exponential function ${e}^{y}.$\n\nLet's denote\n\n$$\nP(x,y)={y}^{3},\\,Q(x,y)=xy.\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=\\,{{field-3}}\n$$\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}=\\,{{field-4}}\n$$\n\nSince for this equation \n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{P}(\\frac{∂P}{∂y}-\\frac{∂Q}{∂x})={{field-5}},\n$$\n\nwhich depends on $y$ only, then an integrating factor for our equation is\n\n$$\nI(y)={{field-6}}.\n$$\n\nand we arrive at the exact equation\n\n$$\n{{field-7}}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14069857/state.json" "file_sha256" "ff78b0778dd4a17d5bed3e2fb18bcca075ccb3c3093b0045d7201edbbea16600"} {"question" "q-318660" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "For a differential equation of the form\n\n$$\nP(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x+Q(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y=0,\n$$\n\nwe have that if\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{P}(\\frac{∂P}{∂y}-\\frac{∂Q}{∂x})=h(y)\n$$\n\nwhere $h(y)$ is independent of $x,$ then an integrating factor for the equation is\n\n$$\nI(y)=\\operatorname{exp}⁡(-\\int h(y)\\,\\text{d}y)\n$$\n\nwhere $\\operatorname{exp}⁡(y)$ denotes the exponential function ${e}^{y}.$\n\nLet's denote\n\n$$\nP(x,y)={y}^{3},\\,Q(x,y)=xy.\n$$\n\nNow, let's compute the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂P}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}({y}^{3})=3{y}^{2} \\\\ \\frac{∂Q}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(xy)=y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{P}(\\frac{∂P}{∂y}-\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}) & =\\frac{1}{{y}^{3}}(3{y}^{2}-y) \\\\  & =3{y}^{-1}-{y}^{-2},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nis a function of $y$ only, we can conclude that an integrating factor for our equation is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I(y) & =\\operatorname{exp}⁡(\\int -(3{y}^{-1}-{y}^{-2})\\,\\text{d}y) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{exp}⁡(-(3\\operatorname{ln}⁡y+1/y)) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{exp}⁡(\\operatorname{ln}⁡{y}^{-3})\\cdot \\operatorname{exp}⁡(-1/y) \\\\  & ={y}^{-3}\\,{e}^{-1/y}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand by multiplying our differential equation by the integrating factor, we have\n\n$$\nI(y)\\cdot ({y}^{3}\\,\\text{d}x+xy\\,\\text{d}y)=I(y)\\cdot 0\n$$\n\nwhich simplifies as\n\n$$\n{y}^{-3}{e}^{-1/y}({y}^{3}\\,\\text{d}x+xy\\,\\text{d}y)=0.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14069857/state.json" "file_sha256" "ff78b0778dd4a17d5bed3e2fb18bcca075ccb3c3093b0045d7201edbbea16600"} {"question" "q-318660" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14069857/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "cf34438f440863bfd1f59612629a7e2f63fdf10496d773c35a5498e71b674d1a"} {"question" "q-318660" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/select "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14069857/state.json" "file_sha256" "ff78b0778dd4a17d5bed3e2fb18bcca075ccb3c3093b0045d7201edbbea16600"} {"question" "q-318660" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{1}{P}(\\frac{∂P}{∂y}+\\frac{∂Q}{∂x})"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{P}(\\frac{∂P}{∂y}-\\frac{∂Q}{∂x})"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{Q}(\\frac{∂P}{∂y}+\\frac{∂Q}{∂x})"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{Q}(\\frac{∂P}{∂y}-\\frac{∂Q}{∂x})"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14069857/state.json" "file_sha256" "ff78b0778dd4a17d5bed3e2fb18bcca075ccb3c3093b0045d7201edbbea16600"} {"question" "q-318660" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{1}{P}(\\frac{∂P}{∂y}-\\frac{∂Q}{∂x})"] "category" "ma_explicit_answer" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14069857/state.json" "file_sha256" "ff78b0778dd4a17d5bed3e2fb18bcca075ccb3c3093b0045d7201edbbea16600"} {"question" "q-318660" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/select "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14069857/state.json" "file_sha256" "ff78b0778dd4a17d5bed3e2fb18bcca075ccb3c3093b0045d7201edbbea16600"} {"question" "q-318660" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\operatorname{exp}⁡(-\\int h(y)\\,\\text{d}y)"] ["math" "\\operatorname{exp}⁡(-h(y))"] ["math" "\\operatorname{exp}⁡(\\int h(x)\\,\\text{d}y)"] ["math" "\\operatorname{exp}⁡(h(y))"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14069857/state.json" "file_sha256" "ff78b0778dd4a17d5bed3e2fb18bcca075ccb3c3093b0045d7201edbbea16600"} {"question" "q-318660" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\operatorname{exp}⁡(-\\int h(y)\\,\\text{d}y)"] "category" "ma_explicit_answer" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14069857/state.json" "file_sha256" "ff78b0778dd4a17d5bed3e2fb18bcca075ccb3c3093b0045d7201edbbea16600"} {"question" "q-3186